1
00:00:01,627 --> 00:00:04,129
I CANNOT BELIEVE
THAT YOU DIDN'T TELL ME

2
00:00:04,171 --> 00:00:05,464
WE ARE
STILL MARRIED.

3
00:00:05,506 --> 00:00:07,424
LOOK, I WAS GOING TO TELL YOU.

4
00:00:07,466 --> 00:00:10,177
WHEN? AFTER THE BIRTH
OF OUR FIRST SECRET CHILD?

5
00:00:10,218 --> 00:00:11,553
ROSS DIDN'T

6
00:00:11,595 --> 00:00:12,554
GET THE ANNULMENT.

7
00:00:12,596 --> 00:00:13,764
WE ARE STILL MARRIED.

8
00:00:13,806 --> 00:00:14,723
WHAT?

9
00:00:14,765 --> 00:00:16,934
OH, MY GOD!

10
00:00:17,977 --> 00:00:19,770
ROSS?

11
00:00:19,812 --> 00:00:21,730
OKAY, MAYBE IT WASN'T
MY BEST DECISION

12
00:00:21,772 --> 00:00:24,274
BUT I JUST COULDN'T FACE
ANOTHER FAILED MARRIAGE.

13
00:00:24,316 --> 00:00:25,526
LET ME JUST
JUMP IN AND ASK.

14
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:26,777
AT WHAT POINT
DID YOU THINK

15
00:00:26,819 --> 00:00:28,278
THIS WAS
A SUCCESSFUL MARRIAGE?

16
00:00:29,989 --> 00:00:31,490
RACH, COME ON.

17
00:00:31,532 --> 00:00:35,369
IF YOU THINK ABOUT IT,
IT'S ACTUALLY KIND OF FUNNY.

18
00:00:36,954 --> 00:00:39,874
MAYBE IT'S BEST
NOT TO THINK ABOUT IT.

19
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,668
THIS IS INEXCUSABLE.

20
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:45,128
I AM SHOCKED TO MY VERY CORE.

21
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:49,090
PHOEBE, I TOLD HER
YOU ALREADY KNEW.

22
00:00:51,844 --> 00:00:53,345
ANOTHER LIE.

23
00:00:53,387 --> 00:00:54,889
YOU HAVE A SICKNESS.

24
00:00:57,182 --> 00:00:58,141
ROSS, JUST FOR
MY OWN PEACE OF MIND

25
00:00:58,183 --> 00:00:59,142
YOU'RE NOT MARRIED

26
00:00:59,184 --> 00:01:01,186
TO ANY MORE
OF US, ARE YOU?

27
00:01:07,568 --> 00:01:12,990
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

28
00:01:13,032 --> 00:01:15,242
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

29
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:17,494
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

30
00:01:17,536 --> 00:01:21,456
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

31
00:01:21,498 --> 00:01:24,752
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

32
00:01:24,793 --> 00:01:27,004
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

33
00:01:27,046 --> 00:01:31,299
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

34
00:01:31,341 --> 00:01:36,889
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

35
00:01:40,099 --> 00:01:42,061
YO, HEY, SOMEONE
LEFT THEIR KEYS.

36
00:01:42,101 --> 00:01:44,396
OOH! TO A PORSCHE, HUH?

37
00:01:44,438 --> 00:01:47,066
HEY, GUNTHER, THESE YOURS?

38
00:01:47,106 --> 00:01:48,650
YEAH, THAT'S WHAT I DRIVE.

39
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,862
I MAKE FOUR BUCKS AN HOUR.

40
00:01:51,904 --> 00:01:53,655
I SAVED UP FOR 350 YEARS.

41
00:01:55,950 --> 00:01:57,451
AW...

42
00:01:57,492 --> 00:02:01,496
HEY, DID ANYBODY
LOSE THEIR KEYS?

43
00:02:01,538 --> 00:02:03,122
JOEY, WHY DON'T
YOU PUT THEM

44
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:04,499
IN THE LOST AND FOUND?

45
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:06,085
THERE'S A LOST AND FOUND?

46
00:02:06,125 --> 00:02:07,753
MY SHOE!

47
00:02:08,796 --> 00:02:11,506
YOU LEFT A SHOE HERE?

48
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:13,550
WELL, I DIDN'T REALIZE
TILL I GOT HOME.

49
00:02:13,592 --> 00:02:15,385
I WASN'T GOING
TO WALK ALL THE WAY

50
00:02:15,427 --> 00:02:17,012
BACK DOWN HERE WITH ONE SHOE.

51
00:02:17,054 --> 00:02:18,931
I'M GOING TO GO
FIND THAT GUY'S CAR

52
00:02:18,973 --> 00:02:20,933
AND LEAVE A NOTE
ON THE WINDSHIELD.

53
00:02:20,975 --> 00:02:22,476
WHEN HE COMES BACK
FOR HIS KEYS

54
00:02:22,517 --> 00:02:24,227
I'LL BE SURE TO
GIVE HIM YOUR SHOE.

55
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:25,604
GREAT. THANKS.

56
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:28,189
OH, GOOD, GOOD.

57
00:02:28,231 --> 00:02:29,483
YOU GUYS ARE HERE.

58
00:02:29,524 --> 00:02:30,818
LISTEN.

59
00:02:30,859 --> 00:02:32,527
HOW WOULD YOU LIKE
TO SPEND TOMORROW

60
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:35,238
TAKING CARE OF THREE
INCREDIBLY CUTE LITTLE PUPPIES?

61
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:37,240
MY GOD! WHAT A FUN DAY.

62
00:02:37,282 --> 00:02:38,784
THAT SOUNDS GREAT.

63
00:02:38,826 --> 00:02:40,285
YEAH, ALL RIGHT.

64
00:02:40,327 --> 00:02:43,122
OKAY. WELL, I'LL
BRING THEM BY
TOMORROW MORNING.

65
00:02:43,162 --> 00:02:45,540
OKAY, AND, UM... BY THE WAY,
THEIR NOT ACTUALLY PUPPIES.

66
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:47,084
THEY'RE FRANK AND ALICE'S
TRIPLETS.

67
00:02:47,126 --> 00:02:48,418
OKAY, SEE YA.

68
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:50,879
WHOA, WHOA, WHOA! WHAT?

69
00:02:50,921 --> 00:02:52,798
PLEASE, PLEASE,
PLEASE, PLEASE,
OH, PLEASE.

70
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:54,257
FRANK AND ALICE
ASKED ME

71
00:02:54,299 --> 00:02:56,093
TO BABY-SIT THE TRIPLETS,
AND I'M NERVOUS.

72
00:02:56,135 --> 00:02:57,886
I'VE NEVER DONE THAT BEFORE
BY MYSELF.

73
00:02:57,928 --> 00:02:59,262
DON'T WORRY
ABOUT IT, PHEEB.

74
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:00,388
WE'LL ABSOLUTELY DO IT.

75
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:01,765
YEAH,
I'M GOING TO PASS

76
00:03:01,807 --> 00:03:03,851
'CAUSE I WAS KIND OF IFFY
WHEN IT WAS PUPPIES.

77
00:03:05,019 --> 00:03:06,937
COME ON,
CHANDLER, COME ON.

78
00:03:06,979 --> 00:03:09,148
IT WILL GIVE US
GREAT PRACTICE

79
00:03:09,188 --> 00:03:12,359
FOR WHEN PEOPLE
WITH BABIES COME TO VISIT.

80
00:03:15,612 --> 00:03:17,072
NICE CAR.

81
00:03:17,114 --> 00:03:19,116
YEAH. IT'S, UH... IT'S NOT MINE.

82
00:03:20,993 --> 00:03:22,327
I LOVE YOUR CAR.

83
00:03:22,369 --> 00:03:24,705
YEAH. IT'S... MINE.

84
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:27,082
I'LL BET IT'S FAST.

85
00:03:27,124 --> 00:03:28,959
ME, TOO. YEAH.

86
00:03:29,001 --> 00:03:30,460
AND COMFORTABLE.

87
00:03:30,502 --> 00:03:33,130
DO YOU, UH... DO YOU
LIKE LEATHER SEATS?

88
00:03:33,172 --> 00:03:33,922
YEAH.

89
00:03:36,215 --> 00:03:37,718
IT'S GOT 'EM.

90
00:03:41,513 --> 00:03:44,975
SO, I STILL
HAVE BOXES HERE

91
00:03:45,017 --> 00:03:48,520
I STILL HAVE
BOXES AT ROSS'

92
00:03:48,562 --> 00:03:50,564
AND I HAVE NOWHERE TO LIVE.

93
00:03:50,605 --> 00:03:53,650
WOW, I CAN SO EASILY
FREAK OUT RIGHT NOW.

94
00:03:53,692 --> 00:03:55,152
OKAY, WHAT ABOUT ME?

95
00:03:55,194 --> 00:03:57,696
I JUST FOUND OUT DENISE
IS LEAVING TOWN FOR A WHILE.

96
00:03:57,738 --> 00:03:59,073
I DON'T HAVE A ROOMMATE.

97
00:04:01,449 --> 00:04:03,410
WELL, MAYBE...

98
00:04:03,451 --> 00:04:06,038
MAYBE I CAN
BE YOUR ROOMMATE, PHEEBS.

99
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:09,541
MAYBE YOU COULD BE MY ROOMMATE.

100
00:04:09,583 --> 00:04:11,543
WELL, THERE'S AN IDEA.

101
00:04:11,585 --> 00:04:12,878
YEAH!

102
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,213
THAT WOULD
BE GREAT!

103
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:15,630
WAIT. HOW LONG
IS DENISE GONE FOR?

104
00:04:15,672 --> 00:04:18,675
UM... SHE SAID SHE'D
BE BACK DECEMBER 26.

105
00:04:18,717 --> 00:04:20,010
OH, DECEMBER 26.

106
00:04:20,052 --> 00:04:21,970
HA! MAYBE SHE'S SANTA CLAUS.

107
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:29,770
OH, LOOK WHO IT IS.

108
00:04:29,811 --> 00:04:31,105
MY HUSBAND.

109
00:04:31,146 --> 00:04:33,065
THE APPLE OF MY EYE.

110
00:04:33,107 --> 00:04:35,192
OKAY, I GOT US
A COURT DATE

111
00:04:35,234 --> 00:04:36,818
FOR TOMORROW AT 2:00

112
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:38,904
AND I PICKED UP ALL THE FORMS.

113
00:04:38,946 --> 00:04:40,906
I'LL TAKE CARE OF EVERYTHING.

114
00:04:40,948 --> 00:04:42,449
WELL, SURE.

115
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:44,451
IF YOU SAY YOU'RE GOING
TO TAKE CARE OF EVERYTHING

116
00:04:44,492 --> 00:04:45,827
I HAVE NO REASON TO DOUBT YOU.

117
00:04:45,869 --> 00:04:47,204
GIVE ME THOSE FORMS.

118
00:04:47,246 --> 00:04:49,915
ALL RIGHT, NOW,
I'M GOING TO
DO THIS MY WAY

119
00:04:49,957 --> 00:04:51,750
AND I DON'T WANT TO HEAR
A PEEP OUT OF YOU.

120
00:04:51,792 --> 00:04:52,751
OKAY, RACH, BUT...

121
00:04:52,793 --> 00:04:54,753
AH! YOU'RE PEEPING.

122
00:04:54,795 --> 00:04:58,423
( mumbling )

123
00:04:58,465 --> 00:04:59,716
ROSS, YOU KNOW WHAT?

124
00:04:59,758 --> 00:05:00,717
I JUST GOT...

125
00:05:00,759 --> 00:05:02,928
WHY? WHY
DID YOU DO THIS?

126
00:05:02,970 --> 00:05:04,345
LOOK, I TOLD YOU I...

127
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:06,265
I DON'T WANT
TO HEAR THREE FAILED MARRIAGES.

128
00:05:06,306 --> 00:05:08,267
LOOK, IF YOU'D HAD
TWO FAILED MARRIAGES

129
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:09,268
YOU'D UNDERSTAND.

130
00:05:09,308 --> 00:05:10,602
WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT?

131
00:05:10,644 --> 00:05:11,603
THANKS TO YOU

132
00:05:11,645 --> 00:05:13,438
I'M HALFWAY THERE.

133
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:17,525
OH! OH, I AM
SO MAD, ROSS.

134
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:19,527
I DON'T THINK
I'VE EVER BEEN THIS ANGRY.

135
00:05:19,569 --> 00:05:23,240
WHAT ABOUT THE TIME
I SAID WE WERE ON A BREAK?

136
00:05:23,282 --> 00:05:24,616
OH!

137
00:05:30,038 --> 00:05:31,330
PHEEB, HOW'S IT GOING?

138
00:05:31,372 --> 00:05:32,332
I'M DOING OKAY.

139
00:05:32,373 --> 00:05:33,374
IT'S GOING WELL.

140
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:34,626
YOU THINK THEY'RE HAVING FUN?

141
00:05:34,668 --> 00:05:35,627
AM I TALKING TOO FAST?

142
00:05:35,669 --> 00:05:37,129
NO. SOUND LIKE ME.

143
00:05:37,171 --> 00:05:38,797
PHEEBS,
IT'S GOING GREAT.

144
00:05:38,839 --> 00:05:41,633
LOOK AT CHANDLER
WITH LITTLE BABY GIRL CHANDLER.

145
00:05:41,675 --> 00:05:43,468
LITTLE BABY GIRL CHANDLER?

146
00:05:43,510 --> 00:05:45,720
WHERE HAVE I HEARD THAT BEFORE?

147
00:05:45,762 --> 00:05:47,472
OH, RIGHT-- COACH RUBIN.

148
00:05:47,514 --> 00:05:49,016
OOH!

149
00:05:51,935 --> 00:05:53,394
YOU KNOW WHAT, PHEEBS?

150
00:05:53,436 --> 00:05:55,022
WHEN YOU'RE DONE OVER THERE

151
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:57,691
WE'VE GOT A KIND
OF SITUATION OVER HERE, TOO.

152
00:05:57,732 --> 00:05:59,067
UH-UH. NO.

153
00:05:59,109 --> 00:06:01,153
WE ARE ALL RESPONSIBLE
FOR OUR OWN BABIES.

154
00:06:01,195 --> 00:06:03,322
SEE, THAT'S WHERE
I THINK THAT YOU'RE WRONG.

155
00:06:03,362 --> 00:06:05,406
WE'VE BEEN PLAYING
THESE BABIES MAN-TO-MAN.

156
00:06:05,448 --> 00:06:07,492
WE SHOULD REALLY
BE PLAYING A ZONE DEFENSE.

157
00:06:07,534 --> 00:06:08,827
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

158
00:06:08,869 --> 00:06:09,870
I JUST THINK

159
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:11,163
THINGS WILL GO A LOT SMOOTHER

160
00:06:11,205 --> 00:06:12,497
IF WE EACH HAVE OUR OWN ZONE.

161
00:06:12,539 --> 00:06:14,291
PHOEBE, YOU CAN
BE IN CHARGE OF WIPING.

162
00:06:14,333 --> 00:06:15,583
AND, YOU KNOW, MON

163
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:17,336
YOU CAN BE IN CHARGE
OF DIAPERING.

164
00:06:17,376 --> 00:06:20,172
AND I CAN BE IN CHARGE
OF LOOKING HOW CUTE THEY ARE

165
00:06:20,214 --> 00:06:22,049
WHEN THEY PUT
THEIR HANDS AROUND...

166
00:06:23,675 --> 00:06:24,968
THAT SOUNDS REALLY GREAT.

167
00:06:25,010 --> 00:06:26,553
MAYBE YOU SHOULD
BE IN CHARGE OF WIPING.

168
00:06:26,594 --> 00:06:27,888
OKAY, I'M A ROOKIE.

169
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:29,681
I SHOULD NOT BE IN THE END ZONE.

170
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:41,651
Monica:
THIS IS SO GREAT.

171
00:06:41,693 --> 00:06:44,696
THIS IS EXACTLY HOW WE SET
THE PLATES AT THE RESTAURANT.

172
00:06:44,738 --> 00:06:45,989
OH, YEAH?

173
00:06:46,031 --> 00:06:47,741
WELL,
THIS IS NOT WHAT I ORDERED.

174
00:06:51,912 --> 00:06:53,372
HEY, GUYS.
HI.
HEY.

175
00:06:53,412 --> 00:06:54,497
HEY, BABIES.

176
00:06:54,539 --> 00:06:56,124
OH, I'M HAVING

177
00:06:56,166 --> 00:06:57,334
THE BEST MORNING.

178
00:06:57,376 --> 00:06:59,169
THAT PORSCHE
I'VE GOT THE KEYS TO--

179
00:06:59,211 --> 00:07:00,587
IT'S STILL THERE.

180
00:07:00,628 --> 00:07:03,422
SHOCKING, SINCE YOU
STILL HAVE THE KEYS.

181
00:07:04,883 --> 00:07:07,969
YOU SHOULD SEE THE TREATMENT
I GET WHEN I'M WITH THAT CAR.

182
00:07:08,011 --> 00:07:10,055
PEOPLE ARE FRIENDLY,
THEY WANT TO TALK

183
00:07:10,097 --> 00:07:11,598
AND NOT JUST ABOUT THE CAR.

184
00:07:11,639 --> 00:07:14,351
ONE GUY GAVE ME ADVICE
ABOUT MY EQUITY INVESTMENTS.

185
00:07:14,393 --> 00:07:15,643
WHAT EQUITY INVESTMENTS?

186
00:07:15,685 --> 00:07:18,063
THE ONES THAT
GOT ME THE PORSCHE.

187
00:07:18,105 --> 00:07:19,606
WILL YOU KEEP UP?

188
00:07:22,025 --> 00:07:24,778
BUT I FIGURED IF PEOPLE KEEP
SEEING ME JUST STANDING THERE

189
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:26,988
THEY'RE GOING TO START
TO THINK I DON'T OWN IT

190
00:07:27,030 --> 00:07:28,656
SO, I FIGURED I'LL WASH IT,
RIGHT?

191
00:07:28,698 --> 00:07:31,159
MONICA, YOU GOT A BUCKET
AND SOME SOAP I CAN BORROW?

192
00:07:31,201 --> 00:07:32,493
OH, YEAH.

193
00:07:32,535 --> 00:07:35,163
I GOT SOAP AND
SPONGES AND RAGS

194
00:07:35,205 --> 00:07:38,708
AND CARNUBA WAX
AND POLISHING COMPOUND.

195
00:07:38,750 --> 00:07:40,752
YOU DON'T EVEN HAVE A CAR.

196
00:07:40,794 --> 00:07:43,255
I KNOW, BUT ONE TIME
THERE WAS THIS REALLY DIRTY CAR

197
00:07:43,297 --> 00:07:45,590
PARKED IN FRONT OF THE BUILDING,
SO I WASHED IT.

198
00:07:45,632 --> 00:07:47,384
AND?

199
00:07:47,426 --> 00:07:49,552
AND SIX OTHERS.

200
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:51,263
THERE YOU ARE.

201
00:07:53,932 --> 00:07:56,101
YEAH, SHE TOPS OUT AT 130.

202
00:07:56,143 --> 00:07:57,269
WOW.

203
00:07:57,311 --> 00:07:58,437
AND THAT'S JUST

204
00:07:58,477 --> 00:07:59,938
IN THE CITY.

205
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:01,440
I GET HER UP TO 160
WHEN I TAKE HER UPSTATE.

206
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:02,649
REALLY?

207
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:03,984
YOU GOT A PLACE UPSTATE?

208
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:05,819
SURE.

209
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:08,780
WELL, I'LL SEE YOU LATER.

210
00:08:08,822 --> 00:08:10,365
OKAY. TAKE IT EASY.

211
00:08:11,950 --> 00:08:14,786
HEY, THAT'S MY CAR.

212
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:16,579
REALLY? OH. UH...

213
00:08:16,621 --> 00:08:18,999
JUST GIVE ME
FIVE MORE MINUTES, WILL YOU?

214
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,959
WHAT...
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

215
00:08:21,001 --> 00:08:22,836
OH, I...
I FOUND THE KEYS

216
00:08:22,877 --> 00:08:25,464
AND NOW I'M JUST
POLISHING HER UP.

217
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:27,466
BUT IT'S MY CAR.

218
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:29,217
YEAH, BUT IT'S MY WAX.

219
00:08:29,259 --> 00:08:33,472
LISTEN, I DON'T COME
TO THE CITY MUCH

220
00:08:33,512 --> 00:08:35,056
AND I DON'T KNOW
IF YOU'RE CRAZY

221
00:08:35,098 --> 00:08:37,267
OR IF THIS IS SOME
KIND OF STREET THEATER...

222
00:08:37,309 --> 00:08:38,768
BUT COULD

223
00:08:38,810 --> 00:08:39,894
I HAVE MY KEYS?

224
00:08:39,936 --> 00:08:41,229
SURE. HERE.

225
00:08:41,271 --> 00:08:43,231
I'LL SAVE YOU A PARKING SPOT.

226
00:08:43,273 --> 00:08:44,565
I'M NOT COMING BACK.

227
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:45,900
WHY NOT?

228
00:08:45,942 --> 00:08:47,194
I LIVE UPSTATE.

229
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:49,363
YEAH, SO DID I.

230
00:08:51,072 --> 00:08:53,158
I DON'T KNOW WHY I WAS
SO NERVOUS ABOUT THIS.

231
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:55,994
AND I DON'T KNOW WHY
FRANK AND ALICE ARE
ALWAYS COMPLAINING.

232
00:08:56,036 --> 00:08:57,536
THIS IS SO EASY.

233
00:08:57,578 --> 00:09:00,081
YEAH, TWO HOURS, A LIFETIME--
THAT'S THE SAME.

234
00:09:01,624 --> 00:09:04,085
CHECK IT OUT. CHECK IT OUT.

235
00:09:04,127 --> 00:09:08,089
WHEN THE BABIES WAKE UP,
THEY CAN MEET KROG.

236
00:09:08,131 --> 00:09:09,590
CHANDLER, WHAT
ARE YOU DOING?

237
00:09:09,632 --> 00:09:11,676
THAT THING COULD PUT
SOMEONE'S EYE OUT.

238
00:09:11,718 --> 00:09:13,512
HE CAN DO MORE THAN THAT.

239
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:15,555
HE CAN DESTROY THE UNIVERSE.

240
00:09:15,596 --> 00:09:19,059
NO. CHANDLER, THEY COULD SWALLOW
ONE OF THOSE LITTLE PARTS.

241
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,061
AND ALSO, LOOK
AT HIS SMOOTH AREA--

242
00:09:21,102 --> 00:09:23,063
THAT'S JUST GOING
TO MESS THEM UP.

243
00:09:23,104 --> 00:09:25,065
LOOK, THEY'RE NOT GOING
TO SWALLOW ANYTHING.

244
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:26,941
YOU GUYS ARE BEING
WAY TOO OVERPROTECTIVE.

245
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:29,027
WHEN I WAS A KID,
MY MOM USED TO JUST THROW ME

246
00:09:29,069 --> 00:09:30,320
INTO A PILE OF BROKEN GLASS.

247
00:09:30,362 --> 00:09:31,946
WHAT?

248
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:33,990
GLASS, SAND, WHATEVER.

249
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:39,413
OH, LOOK AT LITTLE LESLIE
STRETCHING IN HER SLEEP.

250
00:09:39,454 --> 00:09:40,830
OH, IT'S SO CUTE.

251
00:09:40,872 --> 00:09:43,333
I WONDER WHAT AGE IT IS
THAT YOU STOP BEING ABLE

252
00:09:43,375 --> 00:09:45,252
TO PUT BOTH LEGS
BEHIND YOUR HEAD?

253
00:09:45,293 --> 00:09:46,711
OH, I CAN STILL DO THAT.

254
00:09:46,753 --> 00:09:48,380
HOW ARE YOU
STILL SINGLE?

255
00:09:49,923 --> 00:09:51,258
ALL RIGHT.

256
00:09:51,299 --> 00:09:54,094
I'VE THOUGHT ABOUT IT
AND MAYBE YOU'RE RIGHT.

257
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:55,929
MAYBE KROG IS
NOT A SAFE TOY.

258
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:57,180
GOOD. WHAT CHANGED YOUR MIND?

259
00:09:57,222 --> 00:09:59,266
I SWALLOWED HIS
SONIC BLASTER GUN.

260
00:09:59,307 --> 00:10:00,600
Phoebe:
WHAT?

261
00:10:00,641 --> 00:10:01,976
HOW DID THAT HAPPEN?

262
00:10:02,018 --> 00:10:04,229
WELL, I WAS TRYING TO PROVE
THAT I WAS RIGHT.

263
00:10:04,271 --> 00:10:05,230
YOU KNOW, AND

264
00:10:05,272 --> 00:10:06,981
IT TURNS OUT I WAS WRONG

265
00:10:07,023 --> 00:10:11,361
AND... NOW IT'S LODGED
IN MY THROAT.

266
00:10:13,905 --> 00:10:16,032
DAMN IT. YOU KNOW,
THIS WHOLE TIME

267
00:10:16,074 --> 00:10:18,285
WE WERE CONCENTRATING
ON THE BABIES

268
00:10:18,326 --> 00:10:20,412
AND NO ONE WAS WATCHING
CHANDLER.

269
00:10:20,454 --> 00:10:23,164
( gagging )

270
00:10:23,206 --> 00:10:26,042
OKAY, YOU TWO ARE ASKING
THE COURT FOR AN ANNULMENT?

271
00:10:26,084 --> 00:10:27,294
YES, YOUR HONOR

272
00:10:27,335 --> 00:10:29,754
AND HERE ARE OUR FORMS,
ALL FILLED OUT.

273
00:10:29,796 --> 00:10:31,465
SO, BASED ON
YOUR PETITION

274
00:10:31,506 --> 00:10:34,593
YOU ARE SEEKING AN ANNULMENT
ON THE GROUNDS

275
00:10:34,634 --> 00:10:37,304
THAT MR. GELLER
IS MENTALLY UNSTABLE?

276
00:10:39,931 --> 00:10:44,436
FINE. I'M MENTALLY
UNSTABLE.

277
00:10:44,478 --> 00:10:46,104
AND BASED ON THE FACT
THAT MR. GELLER

278
00:10:46,146 --> 00:10:47,439
IS AN INTRAVENOUS DRUG USER?

279
00:10:47,481 --> 00:10:49,608
WHAT?

280
00:10:49,649 --> 00:10:51,943
UH, YES, HEROIN AND CRACK.

281
00:10:53,445 --> 00:10:56,406
CRACK ISN'T EVEN
AN INTRAVENOUS DRUG.

282
00:10:56,448 --> 00:10:58,074
WELL, YOU WOULD KNOW.

283
00:10:59,867 --> 00:11:02,203
NOW, IT ALSO SAYS HERE
THAT YOU, UM

284
00:11:02,245 --> 00:11:05,624
LIED ABOUT YOUR SEXUAL
PREFERENCE BEFORE MARRIAGE.

285
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:06,874
OH, COME ON.

286
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:09,377
ROSS, PLEASE.
I FOUND THE MAGAZINES.

287
00:11:11,963 --> 00:11:13,465
AND FINALLY,
THAT YOU WERE UNABLE

288
00:11:13,507 --> 00:11:14,799
TO CONSUMMATE THE MARRIAGE.

289
00:11:14,841 --> 00:11:16,134
WELL, THAT MAKES SENSE

290
00:11:16,176 --> 00:11:17,760
SINCE YOU'RE GAY
AND ADDICTED TO HEROIN.

291
00:11:17,802 --> 00:11:20,514
OKAY, YOU KNOW,
I'M SORRY...

292
00:11:20,555 --> 00:11:22,098
THIS IS INSANE.

293
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:24,892
I'M NOT ADDICTED TO HEROIN.

294
00:11:24,934 --> 00:11:26,978
I'M NOT GAY
AND THERE IS NO PROBLEM

295
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:28,687
WITH MY ABILITY
TO CONSUMMATE ANYTHING.

296
00:11:28,729 --> 00:11:33,652
LOOK, I'LL CONSUMMATE THIS
MARRIAGE RIGHT HERE, RIGHT NOW.

297
00:11:33,692 --> 00:11:37,030
THAT WON'T BE NECESSARY.

298
00:11:37,071 --> 00:11:39,407
AND WHEN WE WERE DATING,
WE CONSUMMATED LIKE BUNNIES.

299
00:11:39,449 --> 00:11:41,242
AH!

300
00:11:41,284 --> 00:11:44,162
NOW, IF YOU TWO WERE INVOLVED
IN A SERIOUS RELATIONSHIP

301
00:11:44,204 --> 00:11:45,788
THAT REALLY CREATES A PROBLEM.

302
00:11:45,830 --> 00:11:47,207
YOUR HONOR, REST ASSURED

303
00:11:47,248 --> 00:11:49,376
THAT RELATIONSHIP
ENDED TWO YEARS AGO

304
00:11:49,417 --> 00:11:51,628
AND CAN YOU PLEASE STRIKE
"CONSUMMATED LIKE BUNNIES"

305
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:52,629
FROM THE RECORD?

306
00:11:52,671 --> 00:11:55,089
IS THERE ANYTHING IN THIS RECORD

307
00:11:55,131 --> 00:11:56,841
THAT IS ACTUALLY TRUE?

308
00:11:56,883 --> 00:12:00,387
WELL, YES, WE GOT MARRIED
IN VEGAS

309
00:12:00,428 --> 00:12:03,348
AND, UH...
THE NAMES, I THINK.

310
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:05,141
WELL, BASED ON WHAT I'VE HEARD

311
00:12:05,183 --> 00:12:07,935
YOU TWO CERTAINLY DON'T QUALIFY
FOR AN ANNULMENT.

312
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:09,312
IF YOU DON'T WANT
TO BE TOGETHER

313
00:12:09,354 --> 00:12:11,064
YOU'LL HAVE TO FILE FOR DIVORCE.

314
00:12:11,105 --> 00:12:13,066
THAT'S GREAT.
YOU HAPPY NOW?

315
00:12:13,107 --> 00:12:16,361
LOOK WHAT YOU DID WITH
YOUR FUNNY, FUNNY FORM.

316
00:12:16,403 --> 00:12:17,362
WHAT? ME?

317
00:12:17,404 --> 00:12:18,737
WHAT ABOUT YOU

318
00:12:18,779 --> 00:12:20,699
AND YOUR "CONSUMMATED
LIKE BUNNIES" NONSENSE?

319
00:12:20,739 --> 00:12:21,700
IT WAS...

320
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:23,535
WHAT ARE YOU
TYPING THAT FOR?

321
00:12:23,577 --> 00:12:26,413
SHE ALREADY SAID
WE DON'T GET THE ANNULMENT.

322
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:28,665
DON'T TYPE THAT.

323
00:12:28,707 --> 00:12:30,375
STOP TYPING.

324
00:12:30,417 --> 00:12:32,793
HEY. STOP TYPING.

325
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:34,879
STOP TYPING!
STOP TYPING!

326
00:12:34,921 --> 00:12:36,755
OKAY. OKAY.
DO YOU SEE?

327
00:12:36,797 --> 00:12:40,594
DO YOU SEE WHAT YOU'RE
KEEPING ME MARRIED TO?

328
00:12:40,635 --> 00:12:42,470
YOU NEED TO GET OUT
OF MY CHAMBERS.

329
00:12:42,512 --> 00:12:44,598
ALL RIGHT, LOOK, LADY,
HERE IS THE DEAL:

330
00:12:44,639 --> 00:12:46,099
I CAME HERE
FOR AN ANNULMENT

331
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:48,435
AND I AM NOT LEAVING HERE
UNTIL I GET ONE.

332
00:12:48,476 --> 00:12:50,061
WANT TO SPEND
THE NIGHT IN JAIL?

333
00:12:50,103 --> 00:12:52,647
OKAY, THANK YOU
FOR YOUR TIME.

334
00:12:56,109 --> 00:13:00,447
( hoarse screech )

335
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:05,034
( gargles )

336
00:13:05,076 --> 00:13:07,120
( hoarse screech )

337
00:13:14,419 --> 00:13:16,588
SO THAT PORSCHE GUY
TOOK HIS CAR BACK.

338
00:13:19,090 --> 00:13:22,510
BUT YOU FOUND THE KEYS
TO HIS CLOTHES?

339
00:13:22,552 --> 00:13:23,720
NO. I JUST, UH...

340
00:13:23,762 --> 00:13:25,722
I JUST LOVE THE WAY IT FEELS

341
00:13:25,764 --> 00:13:28,391
WHEN EVERYBODY THINKS
I OWN A PORSCHE.

342
00:13:28,433 --> 00:13:31,102
AND PEOPLE WILL THINK
YOU OWN A PORSCHE

343
00:13:31,144 --> 00:13:32,979
BECAUSE YOU'RE
WEARING THE CLOTHES?

344
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:34,314
OF COURSE.

345
00:13:34,355 --> 00:13:35,898
ONLY AN IDIOT
WOULD WEAR THIS STUFF

346
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,275
IF HE DIDN'T HAVE THE CAR.

347
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:42,405
THAT IS TRUE.

348
00:13:42,447 --> 00:13:46,326
YEAH, BUT ONLY A GENIUS WOULD
SWALLOW A SONIC BLASTER GUN.

349
00:13:46,367 --> 00:13:48,369
OH, I'VE BEEN THERE.

350
00:13:49,912 --> 00:13:53,832
WELL, I AM GOING TO GO DRIVE
MY PORSCHE.

351
00:13:53,874 --> 00:13:56,503
JOEY, YOU KNOW YOU DON'T
ACTUALLY HAVE ONE.

352
00:13:56,544 --> 00:13:58,171
COME ON.
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

353
00:13:58,212 --> 00:13:59,213
I'M IN CHARACTER.

354
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:00,590
WILL YOU TALK TO HER?

355
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:03,426
AH, I THINK IT JUST MOVED.

356
00:14:03,468 --> 00:14:04,678
IT'S REALLY POKING ME.

357
00:14:04,719 --> 00:14:05,886
ALL RIGHT, THAT'S IT.

358
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:07,430
WE'RE GOING
TO THE EMERGENCY ROOM.

359
00:14:07,472 --> 00:14:09,641
WHAT? NO, YOU CAN'T
LEAVE ME HERE WITH THEM.

360
00:14:09,683 --> 00:14:10,642
WE'RE BABY-SITTING.

361
00:14:10,684 --> 00:14:11,810
THE BABIES ARE ASLEEP.

362
00:14:11,850 --> 00:14:13,603
I'M SURE YOU'LL BE
OKAY FOR A WHILE.

363
00:14:13,645 --> 00:14:15,271
BUT YOU CAN'T LEAVE ME
WITH THEM.

364
00:14:15,313 --> 00:14:17,106
WE'RE A TEAM.
WE'RE PLAYING A ZONE.

365
00:14:17,148 --> 00:14:18,817
THEY'RE GOING TO TRIPLE-TEAM ME.

366
00:14:18,857 --> 00:14:21,695
HE'S GOT SOMETHING PLASTIC
LODGED INTO HIS THROAT.

367
00:14:21,736 --> 00:14:23,530
WE'VE GOT TO GO
TO THE HOSPITAL.

368
00:14:23,571 --> 00:14:26,199
BUT, NO, BECAUSE A DOCTOR
WON'T BE ABLE TO HELP HIM.

369
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,950
IT'S JUST GOING TO, YOU KNOW

370
00:14:27,992 --> 00:14:31,078
NATURALLY PASS THROUGH HIS
SYSTEM IN, LIKE, SEVEN YEARS.

371
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:33,331
I THINK THAT'S GUM.

372
00:14:33,373 --> 00:14:35,375
I'M PRETTY SURE
IT'S GUN.

373
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:39,045
OKAY, LISTEN, THIS
REALLY HURTS. LET'S GO.

374
00:14:39,086 --> 00:14:43,216
BUT NO, A REAL MAN WOULDN'T
JUST RUN TO THE HOSPITAL.

375
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:45,092
NO... WHAT WOULD KROG DO?

376
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:52,225
OH, WHY ISN'T THAT VALET
BACK WITH MY PORSCHE?

377
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:55,603
MAYBE BECAUSE
YOU'VE GOT THE KEYS.

378
00:14:57,522 --> 00:14:59,232
PORSCHE.

379
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:02,736
THAT WAS TOTALLY YOUR FAULT.

380
00:15:02,777 --> 00:15:03,737
MY FAULT?

381
00:15:03,778 --> 00:15:05,321
YOU THREATENED THE JUDGE.

382
00:15:05,363 --> 00:15:06,531
WELL, YOU RIPPED
THE PAPER

383
00:15:06,573 --> 00:15:08,241
OUT OF THE COURT
REPORTER'S MACHINE.

384
00:15:08,282 --> 00:15:10,910
THAT WAS THE ONLY WAY
I COULD GET HIM TO STOP TYPING!

385
00:15:10,951 --> 00:15:11,911
OH.

386
00:15:11,952 --> 00:15:14,372
HI. HOW ARE THE GELLERS?

387
00:15:17,876 --> 00:15:21,462
DON'T CALL US THAT.

388
00:15:21,504 --> 00:15:25,132
THE JUDGE WOULDN'T LET
US GET AN ANNULMENT.

389
00:15:25,174 --> 00:15:27,468
NOW WE GOT TO
GET A DIVORCE!

390
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:30,012
DID A PORSCHE
THROW UP ON YOU?

391
00:15:32,432 --> 00:15:36,102
HEY, THAT'S PORSCH-AH!

392
00:15:36,143 --> 00:15:40,398
LOOK AT ME TAKING CARE OF YOU
WITH NO PROBLEM, HUH?

393
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:42,609
YOU GUYS FEEL SAFE, RIGHT?

394
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:45,944
OKAY, I'M GOING TO TAKE THAT
SPIT-BUBBLE AS A "YEAH, I DO."

395
00:15:45,986 --> 00:15:48,114
OKAY, LET'S GET RID OF THIS
DIRTY DIAPER, LESLIE.

396
00:15:48,155 --> 00:15:50,949
I'LL SET YOU UP
WITH A NICE CLEAN ONE.

397
00:15:50,991 --> 00:15:52,201
OKAY, I'M SORRY.

398
00:15:52,243 --> 00:15:54,287
I DIDN'T MEAN TO SCARE YOU.

399
00:15:54,328 --> 00:15:56,790
I JUST HAVE TO CLEAN
THAT UP, OKAY?

400
00:15:56,831 --> 00:15:59,709
'CAUSE, LET'S FACE IT,
WE'RE AT MONICA'S.

401
00:15:59,751 --> 00:16:01,252
OKAY. I BROKE IT.

402
00:16:01,294 --> 00:16:04,631
ALL RIGHT, WELL, THAT'S JUST
THE WAY THINGS GO.

403
00:16:04,672 --> 00:16:07,884
OKAY. GOOD.

404
00:16:07,926 --> 00:16:09,594
WHY ARE THERE ONLY TWO OF YOU?

405
00:16:09,636 --> 00:16:10,845
WHERE'S LESLIE?

406
00:16:10,887 --> 00:16:12,972
WELL, YOU CAN'T ANSWER.

407
00:16:13,013 --> 00:16:15,683
LESLIE, WHERE ARE YOU, LESLIE?

408
00:16:15,725 --> 00:16:19,019
LESLIE, NOW WOULD BE A GOOD
TIME FOR YOUR FIRST WORDS.

409
00:16:19,061 --> 00:16:20,605
( murmurs )

410
00:16:20,647 --> 00:16:23,065
WELL, LOOK AT YOU.

411
00:16:23,107 --> 00:16:25,234
HEY...

412
00:16:25,276 --> 00:16:28,237
YOU ARE A LITTLE BIT
MISCHIEVOUS.

413
00:16:28,279 --> 00:16:29,280
MY GOSH.

414
00:16:29,322 --> 00:16:31,741
OH, YOU'RE A LOT MISCHIEVOUS.

415
00:16:31,783 --> 00:16:33,117
WELL, IT'LL DRY.

416
00:16:33,159 --> 00:16:35,244
ALL RIGHT, LET'S GO PLAY.

417
00:16:35,286 --> 00:16:38,581
YOU SIT WITH YOUR BROTHER
AND SISTER NOW

418
00:16:38,623 --> 00:16:41,041
WHO AREN'T THERE.

419
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:54,388
HI.

420
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:56,349
HOW DO YOU FEEL?

421
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:58,016
WELL, I SHOULD SAY THAT KROG

422
00:16:58,058 --> 00:16:59,602
WILL BE FULLY EQUIPPED

423
00:16:59,644 --> 00:17:02,355
TO DESTROY THE UNIVERSE AGAIN
IN 12 TO 14 HOURS.

424
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:03,898
OKAY.

425
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:06,901
SO, I TOTALLY TOOK
CARE OF THE BABIES
ALL BY MYSELF.

426
00:17:06,943 --> 00:17:09,028
I FED THEM, BATHED THEM
AND PUT THEM TO BED.

427
00:17:09,069 --> 00:17:12,198
AND PROTECTED THEM
FROM A TORNADO?

428
00:17:15,368 --> 00:17:16,911
OH, MY GOD.

429
00:17:16,953 --> 00:17:20,164
I KNOW.
THE BABIES ARE ASLEEP.

430
00:17:20,206 --> 00:17:21,875
PHOEBE, WHAT HAPPENED HERE?

431
00:17:21,916 --> 00:17:23,209
I DID IT.

432
00:17:23,250 --> 00:17:25,503
I TOOK CARE OF THE BABIES
ALL BY MYSELF.

433
00:17:25,545 --> 00:17:26,880
B-B-BUT MY APARTMENT?

434
00:17:26,921 --> 00:17:27,881
WAS THE SETTING

435
00:17:27,922 --> 00:17:29,757
OF PHOEBE'S TRIUMPH.

436
00:17:31,009 --> 00:17:32,468
BUT THE MESS...

437
00:17:32,510 --> 00:17:34,136
IS NOT AS IMPORTANT
AS THE FACT

438
00:17:34,178 --> 00:17:36,430
THAT PHOEBE TOOK CARE
OF THE BABIES ALL BY HERSELF.

439
00:17:36,472 --> 00:17:37,598
YOU'RE RIGHT.

440
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:39,308
YOU'RE RIGHT,
I SHOULDN'T FREAK OUT

441
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:41,435
'CAUSE THIS IS WHAT
IT'S GOING TO BE LIKE

442
00:17:41,477 --> 00:17:42,896
WHEN YOU AND I HAVE BABIES.

443
00:17:42,937 --> 00:17:43,938
WHEN WILL THAT BE?

444
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:49,193
WOULD YOU TAKE A
LOOK AT THIS MESS?

445
00:17:57,117 --> 00:17:59,245
OH, HONEY,
THANK GOD YOU'RE HOME.

446
00:17:59,286 --> 00:18:00,747
I WAS GETTING WORRIED.

447
00:18:00,788 --> 00:18:03,416
I PICKED UP THE DIVORCE PAPERS.

448
00:18:03,457 --> 00:18:06,293
UH, I'VE ALREADY
SIGNED EVERYTHING

449
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:10,089
AND I PUT LITTLE X's
WHERE YOU NEED TO SIGN.

450
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:11,424
OH, LITTLE X's... GREAT.

451
00:18:11,465 --> 00:18:13,175
THAT MAKES UP
FOR EVERYTHING.

452
00:18:13,217 --> 00:18:18,806
YOU KNOW, YOU'VE DONE A LOT
OF STUPID STUFF, TOO, OKAY?

453
00:18:18,848 --> 00:18:21,851
OH, NAME ONE STUPID THING
THAT IS AS STUPID AS THIS ONE.

454
00:18:21,893 --> 00:18:24,437
OKAY, HOW ABOUT YOU FLEW
TO LONDON TO STOP MY WEDDING.

455
00:18:24,478 --> 00:18:26,230
UH, HOW ABOUT YOU TOLD ME
YOU LOVED ME

456
00:18:26,272 --> 00:18:27,565
AFTER I WAS ALREADY MARRIED.

457
00:18:27,607 --> 00:18:28,566
HEY, WAIT A MINUTE.

458
00:18:28,608 --> 00:18:30,109
THAT WAS DIFFERENT.

459
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:32,445
I DID THOSE THINGS
BECAUSE I WAS IN LOVE WITH YOU.

460
00:18:32,486 --> 00:18:34,530
YEAH, RIGHT.

461
00:18:36,198 --> 00:18:39,410
YOU'RE RIGHT.
THAT'S VERY DIFFERENT.

462
00:18:39,452 --> 00:18:43,081
SO, LET'S...
LET'S JUST SIGN THE PAPERS.

463
00:18:45,291 --> 00:18:46,793
WHAT?

464
00:18:46,834 --> 00:18:48,294
NOTHING.

465
00:18:48,335 --> 00:18:51,631
OKAY, CAN WE JUST
SIGN, PLEASE?

466
00:18:51,672 --> 00:18:54,258
MM-HMM.

467
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:05,561
CONGRATULATIONS.

468
00:19:05,603 --> 00:19:06,562
OKAY, WAIT, ROSS.

469
00:19:06,604 --> 00:19:07,814
WAIT A MINUTE. UM...

470
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:09,189
I, UH...

471
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:12,068
KIND OF HAVE
A LITTLE CONFESSION.

472
00:19:12,110 --> 00:19:13,778
WHAT?

473
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:17,406
UH, WELL, YOU KNOW THIS WHOLE
MARRIAGE THING...

474
00:19:17,448 --> 00:19:18,699
KIND OF MY IDEA.

475
00:19:18,741 --> 00:19:21,410
EXCUSE ME?

476
00:19:21,452 --> 00:19:23,245
UH, WELL, REMEMBER
HOW WE WERE TOO DRUNK

477
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:25,498
TO REMEMBER ANYTHING
THE NIGHT WE WERE MARRIED?

478
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:26,499
YEAH.

479
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:27,834
AND, UH...

480
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:30,252
YEAH, I DIDN'T WANT
TO SAY ANYTHING

481
00:19:30,294 --> 00:19:32,171
BUT IT JUST KEPT
COMING BACK TO ME

482
00:19:32,212 --> 00:19:34,340
AND, UM, REMEMBER
WE WERE IN THE CASINO

483
00:19:34,381 --> 00:19:36,258
AND FOR SOME REASON
YOU THOUGHT

484
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:38,427
IT WOULD BE FUNNY
TO EAT A LOT OF GRAPES?

485
00:19:38,469 --> 00:19:40,888
AND, UH, AND I THOUGHT

486
00:19:40,930 --> 00:19:44,183
IT WOULD BE FUNNIER
IF WE GOT MARRIED.

487
00:19:44,224 --> 00:19:48,771
SO, AS A COMPROMISE,
WE DECIDED FIRST TO GET MARRIED

488
00:19:48,813 --> 00:19:50,106
AND THEN...

489
00:19:50,148 --> 00:19:53,151
Both:
TO EAT A LOT OF GRAPES.

490
00:19:53,192 --> 00:19:59,866
SO, UM, SORRY I GOT US
INTO THIS WHOLE THING.

491
00:19:59,907 --> 00:20:03,744
SO, THEN, I MEAN, IF
YOU THINK ABOUT IT

492
00:20:03,786 --> 00:20:06,122
THIS IS ALL YOUR FAULT.

493
00:20:06,164 --> 00:20:10,626
YEAH, DON'T PUSH IT THOUGH.

494
00:20:10,668 --> 00:20:17,466
I GOT TO SAY, I KNOW I DIVORCE
A LOT OF WOMEN.

495
00:20:19,886 --> 00:20:23,597
NEVER THOUGHT
I'D BE DIVORCING YOU.

496
00:20:23,639 --> 00:20:25,016
I KNOW.

497
00:20:25,058 --> 00:20:27,560
I ALWAYS THOUGHT
IF YOU AND I GOT MARRIED

498
00:20:27,601 --> 00:20:29,854
THAT WOULD BE THE ONE
THAT STUCK.

499
00:20:29,896 --> 00:20:31,856
AND IT WOULDN'T BE A SECRET.

500
00:20:31,898 --> 00:20:35,568
AND WE WOULDN'T HAVE
OUR WEDDING DINNER AT PIZZA HUT.

501
00:20:35,609 --> 00:20:40,406
OH... DID I...
DID I EVEN TREAT?

502
00:20:40,447 --> 00:20:42,282
NO, IT WAS ON THE HOUSE.

503
00:20:42,324 --> 00:20:44,368
IT WAS A NEWLYWED SPECIAL.

504
00:20:44,410 --> 00:20:47,788
THAT MAY BE THE MOST DEPRESSING
THING I'VE HEARD IN MY LIFE.

505
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:49,665
YEAH.

506
00:20:49,707 --> 00:20:53,544
I SHOULD PROBABLY GET THESE
TO MY LAWYER'S OFFICE.

507
00:20:53,586 --> 00:20:55,088
YEAH-- HEY, THANKS, ROSS

508
00:20:55,129 --> 00:20:56,797
FOR TAKING CARE
OF ALL THIS.

509
00:20:56,839 --> 00:20:58,091
AH, NO PROBLEM.

510
00:21:08,851 --> 00:21:10,352
I'M GOING TO NEED
A COPY OF THOSE.

511
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:11,812
TOTALLY.
YEAH.

512
00:21:17,944 --> 00:21:22,782
HEY! HEY!
CAREFUL AROUND MY PORSCHE.

513
00:21:22,823 --> 00:21:24,283
HI, JOEY.

514
00:21:24,324 --> 00:21:27,285
HEY, HOW YOU DOING?

515
00:21:27,327 --> 00:21:30,456
HE HAS THE MOST AMAZING
PORSCHE UNDER THERE.

516
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:32,708
I'D LOVE TO SHOW YOU,
BUT I JUST TUCKED HER IN.

517
00:21:32,750 --> 00:21:33,751
SHE'S SLEEPING.

518
00:21:33,793 --> 00:21:35,211
( giggles )

519
00:21:35,253 --> 00:21:37,504
HEY, WOULD YOU TWO GIRLS
LIKE TO GO FOR A DRINK?

520
00:21:42,843 --> 00:21:45,846
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

